From 434a9b068d898451a8497b2ab360d223106ff8bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wranked1 <129415993+Wranked1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 11:01:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix chat preview message background not matching its text

With some combinations of resolution, chat font size and chat width,
a message background in the chat settings preview was sized as if the
text wrapped to a second line although the text was rendered on a
single line (or vice versa), which also shifted all following
backgrounds. For example at 1920x1080 with font size 100 and width 263
the "Spammer" line got a two line background.

Since fee9b986f the preview measures each message for its background
by laying out the text at position (0, 0), but renders the text at the
actual preview position. The text renderer aligns the start of the
text to the screen pixel grid while the line width is compared against
the unaligned start position, so line wrapping and the measured width
depend on the position by up to a fraction of a pixel. A word that
ends right at the line width limit can then wrap in the measurement
but not when rendering.

Measure the message at the same position that it is rendered at, so
the background always matches the rendered text. The ingame chat
already measures at the same x position that it renders at.

Closes #8179.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E3rsC3FRVop9j9KaM9zRGS
---
 src/game/client/components/menus_settings_appearance.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/game/client/components/menus_settings_appearance.cpp b/src/game/client/components/menus_settings_appearance.cpp
index 8b67015cc..b5a334674 100644
--- a/src/game/client/components/menus_settings_appearance.cpp
+++ b/src/game/client/components/menus_settings_appearance.cpp
@@ -436,7 +436,7 @@ void CMenus::RenderSettingsAppearance(CUIRect MainView)
 			const float RealBackgroundRounding = Chat.MessageRounding() * 2.0f;
 
 			auto &&RenderMessageBackground = [&](int LineIndex) {
-				auto Size = RenderPreview(LineIndex, 0, 0, false);
+				auto Size = RenderPreview(LineIndex, X, TempY, false);
 				Graphics()->DrawRectExt(X - RealMsgPaddingX / 2.0f, TempY - RealMsgPaddingY / 2.0f, Size.x + RealMsgPaddingX * 1.5f, Size.y, RealBackgroundRounding, IGraphics::CORNER_ALL);
 				return Size.y;
 			};
